# MOVE - Move files between locations

```text
MOVE source destination
```

## Move a file

Give the destination drive/user to keep the filename, or supply a new
name. The resident command copies to the destination before erasing the
original. An existing destination blocks the move.

```text
MOVE A0:NOTES.TXT D3:
```

## Move a group

```text
DIR B1:*.DOC
MOVE B1:*.DOC D3:
```

Inspect the selection first. Moving a group processes individual files.
Use [COPY](COPY.HLP) when the originals should stay where they are.
